  "body": "Currently [fetch a modulepreload module script graph](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#fetch-a-modulepreload-module-script-graph) optionally proceeds to steps to fetch the descendants of the preloaded module without checking the result of [fetch a single module script](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#fetch-a-single-module-script) for failure.  It doesn't make sense to try to fetch descendants if the original fetch failed (e.g. due to 404), and [fetch the descendants of and link](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#fetch-the-descendants-of-and-link-a-module-script)  doesn't expect to be passed a null `module script`.\r\n\r\nThus, this change guards the optional steps with a null check.\r\n\r\nThis clarification should be a no-op for implementers, who must already have this sort of check in place; there's not much that they could do otherwise.",
